Dear Ines

Kestrel Software Ltd – Series A completed

Congratulations to you and Tobias. Completion took place this morning and, as you confirmed, the £4,000,000 was in Kestrel's bank account by 11:20.

What was signed today:

1. the subscription agreement between Kestrel, you and Tobias, Merrowdown and Pellridge, dated 23 October 2026, under which Merrowdown has 1,875,000 Series A shares and Pellridge 625,000, at £1.60 each;
2. the disclosure letter;
3. the minutes of Kestrel's board meeting at 10:30, which approved the agreement, allotted the shares and appointed Felix Amberley as a director; and
4. the shareholders' written resolution adopting the new articles.

The executed copies of the agreement and the minutes are in the Executed folder of your matter on our document system, and I will email you a complete set next week.

What is left to do:

1. Share certificates for Merrowdown and Pellridge, and bringing Kestrel's registers up to date. Jamie will prepare them and send them to you for signature.
2. The filings at the companies registry: the return of allotment, the new articles and Felix's appointment. They must go in within the time the law allows. Jamie will file them early next week so that we are well inside it.
3. The originals of Owain Rhys's IP assignment. We hold a copy, and Tobias is to chase Owain for the originals.
4. Replacing the open-source component in the desktop app that has the copyleft licence, by 31 March 2027, as you have promised the investors. Please tell me before the next release of the app is sent to anyone.

Thank you both for the speed with which you answered the investors' questions, which made a tight timetable possible. Thanks too to Priya, Jamie and Chris, who did a great deal of the work behind this.

